WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:17.293
Dr. Dolittle was not at all as Tommy had imagined.

2
00:00:17.294 --> 00:00:20.546
He did not look like an amazing animal doctor.

3
00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:23.356
And he did not look like a world traveler.

4
00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:28.872
But he was very kind and certainly seemed to love his animals.

5
00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:32.218
"What's your name?" Dr. Dolittle asked.

6
00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:34.967
"Tommy Stubbins, sir," he answered.

7
00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.762
"Are you the son of the shoemaker?" the doctor asked.

8
00:00:38.763 --> 00:00:41.998
"Yes, sir," Tommy giggled.

9
00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:47.186
The pig was trying to climb on the doctor's lap.

10
00:00:47.187 --> 00:00:51.939
"Get off! Can't you see the doctor is tired?" Jip barked.

11
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.616
"But I want to show Dr. Dolittle my toe.

12
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:56.169
I hurt it yesterday."

13
00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.469
Gub-Gub stuck out a foot.

14
00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:03.117
"Hmm . . . it doesn't look serious, Gub-Gub," said the doctor.

15
00:01:03.118 --> 00:01:05.372
"You just need some cream on it.

16
00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:08.693
Oh, would you mind bringing me my bag?"

17
00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:11.880
Tommy carried the bag over to the doctor.

18
00:01:11.881 --> 00:01:15.505
"Can you really talk to animals?" Tommy whispered.

19
00:01:15.506 --> 00:01:17.696
"Why, yes, of course.

20
00:01:17.697 --> 00:01:20.095
Now where did that cream go?"

21
00:01:20.096 --> 00:01:23.222
Dr. Dolittle poked around in his bag.

22
00:01:23.223 --> 00:01:25.265
He handed Tommy a jar.

23
00:01:25.266 --> 00:01:27.893
The jar was half full of water.

24
00:01:27.894 --> 00:01:31.841
Inside was a funny creature swimming around.

25
00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:36.973
"Dr. Dolittle, what's this?" said Tommy, lifting the jar.

26
00:01:36.974 --> 00:01:40.451
"That is called a wiff-waff," he answered.

27
00:01:40.452 --> 00:01:44.296
Tommy had never heard of a wiff-waff before.

28
00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:48.588
"It's a creature related to the shellfish," the doctor explained.

29
00:01:48.589 --> 00:01:51.396
"That's the language I'm trying to learn at the moment."

30
00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:53.556
The doctor frowned.

31
00:01:53.557 --> 00:01:57.021
"But shellfish talk is very difficult."

32
00:01:57.022 --> 00:01:59.386
"You mean this thing has a language?"

33
00:01:59.387 --> 00:02:02.205
Tommy pointed to the creature.

34
00:02:02.206 --> 00:02:06.289
"All living things have a language," said Dr. Dolittle.

35
00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.896
"How can you learn their language?" Tommy asked.

36
00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:14.756
"It takes a lot of patience and careful attention," the doctor replied.

37
00:02:14.757 --> 00:02:18.202
"Doctor! My toe!" Gub-Gub oinked.

38
00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:21.200
"Sorry, Gub-Gub. Here we are."

39
00:02:21.201 --> 00:02:26.782
The doctor opened another jar and put some cream on the pig's toe.

40
00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:28.364
Tommy was thoughtful.

41
00:02:28.365 --> 00:02:32.469
He wondered if Dr. Dolittle could help the wounded squirrel.

42
00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.191
"Can you speak squirrel language?" he finally asked.

43
00:02:36.192 --> 00:02:37.609
The doctor smiled.

44
00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.709
"Of course. It's very easy to learn."

45
00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:49.432
So Tommy told the doctor all about the squirrel, and the doctor agreed to come look at the sick animal.

46
00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:53.663
Suddenly the duck burst into the room, quacking loudly.

47
00:02:53.664 --> 00:02:56.235
The doctor jumped up in surprise.

48
00:02:56.236 --> 00:03:00.279
"Dab-Dab! What's the matter?" he shouted.

49
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:06.222
The duck waved his wings wildly and squawked.

50
00:03:06.223 --> 00:03:10.359
Tommy wondered what the duck was saying.

51
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:16.611
"Oh, this is a dream come true!" the doctor clapped his hands.

52
00:03:16.612 --> 00:03:19.524
He turned to Tommy and said excitedly,

53
00:03:19.525 --> 00:03:23.781
"My oldest and dearest friend has returned from Africa."

54
00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:25.789
Tommy smiled politely.

55
00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.579
"Come! You must meet Polynesia."

56
00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.709
Everyone followed the duck into the kitchen.

57
00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.159
Tommy looked around but could not see Dr. Dolittle's friend.

58
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.139
"Polynesia!" called the doctor.

59
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:45.173
The doctor ran toward a large parrot sitting on a chair.

60
00:03:45.174 --> 00:03:49.642
The doctor's dearest friend was a bird!

61
00:03:49.643 --> 00:03:56.455
Although Tommy could not understand animal language, he knew everyone was excited to see the parrot.

62
00:03:56.456 --> 00:04:00.675
"Who is that, doctor?" Polynesia looked at Tommy.

63
00:04:00.676 --> 00:04:04.153
"That's Tommy," the doctor answered.

64
00:04:04.154 --> 00:04:09.883
"Hello, Tommy," the parrot suddenly called out to him.

65
00:04:09.884 --> 00:04:12.031
Tommy's eyes opened wide.

66
00:04:12.032 --> 00:04:14.508
His heart started to beat faster.

67
00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:17.812
He clearly understood the parrot's language!

68
00:04:17.813 --> 00:04:20.347
"Dr. Dolittle?" he called out.

69
00:04:20.348 --> 00:04:21.816
"What's wrong, Tommy?

70
00:04:21.817 --> 00:04:26.747
You look pale!" the doctor said worriedly.

71
00:04:26.748 --> 00:04:29.186
"I . . . I understood the bird.

72
00:04:29.187 --> 00:04:33.740
I understood," Tommy replied in an excited voice.

73
00:04:33.741 --> 00:04:40.920
Dr. Dolittle and Polynesia looked at each other.

74
00:04:40.921 --> 00:04:42.780
"Of course, you did, Tommy.

75
00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:49.067
I spoke to you in human language!" Polynesia laughed.

76
00:04:49.068 --> 00:04:51.732
Tommy looked disappointed.

77
00:04:51.733 --> 00:04:56.357
"Polynesia is the best teacher," Dr. Dolittle praised.

78
00:04:56.358 --> 00:04:59.499
"Maybe she can teach you some animal languages."

79
00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.728
Tommy nodded eagerly.

80
00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:04.103
"First I need to eat something,"

81
00:05:04.104 --> 00:05:07.047
Polynesia said and rubbed her stomach.

82
00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:09.572
"It's good to see you again, my friend."

83
00:05:09.573 --> 00:05:15.192
Dr. Dolittle smiled at the parrot.
